-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SteVe — GPL-3.0-or-later
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    https://github.com/steve-community/steve

The `steve.war` shipped in this image is compiled from an UNMODIFIED upstream
release tag. The Dockerfile performs:

    git clone --depth 1 --branch ${STEVE_REF} \
        https://github.com/steve-community/steve.git

No patch, no override, no vendored change is applied. The exact tag used for a
given image is recorded in its `org.opencontainers.image.version` label:

    docker inspect --format '{{ index .Config.Labels "org.opencontainers.image.version" }}' \
        ghcr.io/juherr/steve:<tag>

GPLv3 section 6 requires that the corresponding source accompany the object
code. It is satisfied here by section 6(d): the complete corresponding source of
the exact revision is publicly available, at no charge, from the upstream
repository at the tag named above. The complete build recipe used to produce the
binary — this Dockerfile — is published in this repository.

The `.war` also embeds SteVe's own Maven dependencies, each retaining its
original license.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Flyway CLI (Open Source Edition) — Apache-2.0
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    https://github.com/flyway/flyway
    https://hub.docker.com/r/flyway/flyway

Copied unmodified from the `flyway/flyway` image, which is the Open Source
Edition. It is distinct from Redgate's commercial `redgate/flyway` image, which
is the one requiring a license key and EULA acceptance.

The Flyway CLI is used as a separate program, in a separate process, before
SteVe starts: it replays SteVe's schema migrations against the runtime database.
There is no linking between it and SteVe — this is mere aggregation.

That upstream image also bundles a Java runtime and a set of JDBC drivers, each
under its own license; refer to the `flyway/flyway` image for their terms.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Eclipse Temurin JRE — GPL-2.0 WITH Classpath-exception-2.0
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    https://adoptium.net/

Two independent runtimes are present:
  - the image's own JRE (`eclipse-temurin`), which runs SteVe;
  - the JRE bundled inside the Flyway CLI, which runs Flyway.

The Classpath Exception permits linking application code without extending the
GPL to that application.


